# Light infantry: open order, every man his own shot from behind whatever is there.
# Retuned 2026-10-05 after trials (2-158 became 98-62): a pressing skirmish line - it gives ground
# before a charge and comes back, moves up when it is winning, harries a broken enemy, steps out of
# its own smoke, and shoots from the open when it must.
drill "Skirmishers"
about "Open order, every man in cover and firing at will; gives ground before a charge and comes back; presses when winning, harries the broken."
type Marksman
dials aggression 0.5 discipline 0.35 cohesion 0.15 cover 0.95 patience 0.4 nerve 0.55

sergeant:
  when enemy breaking or enemy broken      -> advance fast; form skirmish; fire at will
  when enemy charging and enemy within 35  -> fall back 25; form skirmish
  when winning the exchange                -> advance slow; find cover; form skirmish; fire at will
  when losing the exchange                 -> fall back 15; find cover; form skirmish; fire at will
  when enemy beyond 60                     -> advance; find cover; form skirmish; fire at will
  otherwise                                -> hold; find cover; form skirmish; fire at will

man:
  when enemy within 6                      -> bayonet
  when enemy charging and enemy within 25 and loaded -> fire; back 10
  when enemy charging and enemy within 25  -> back 15
  when in smoke and enemy beyond 20        -> step out of the smoke
  when loaded and enemy within 80 and ( in cover or on high ground ) -> fire
  when not in cover and enemy within 80    -> take cover within 15
  when not loaded                          -> reload kneeling
  when loaded and enemy within 55          -> fire
  otherwise                                -> follow sergeant
